    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe new test `AcceptanceTest.coreEnqueuesWelcome` captures the logger named `NOTIFY` and asserts that after a successful owner create, some line contains both the owner id and the memberId.\n\nI implemented this in `RespondWithOwnerCreated` \u2014 the pipeline's final `respond` step, reached only on a successful 201 create. It already holds the fully-built `owner` (with id and memberId assigned) and was the natural, guaranteed-on-success point to emit the notification.\n\nTwo lines added:\n- a class-level `NOTIFY` logger (mirroring the existing `AUDIT` logger),\n- `NOTIFY.info(\"welcome ownerId={} memberId={}\", owner.getId(), owner.getMemberId());` just before sending the response.\n\n**Structural-impact reasoning:** `RespondWithOwnerCreated` is a single-method class, so `WMC_other` \u2248 0 (clamped to 1) and the `service` method's CC is 1. Adding one emission line keeps `changed_lines` minimal, and it touches a single file \u2014 cost \u2248 1\u00d71\u00d72 = 2. An alternative new-step-plus-YAML-wiring approach would have touched two files and cost several times more. No existing behaviour changed; the audit lines and response are untouched.\n\n`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.",
